     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Block browserStore:credentialAccess and fileServer:lateralMovement. Blocking browserStore kills jumpHost directly, kills ssoLogin (an AND node that needs it), and kills rdpLogin (also AND). That cuts shareMount, vaultRead and mailArchive, since hypervisor needs ssoLogin. It also kills serviceAccount, because rdpLogin is dead. Blocking fileServer removes the last route to dbReplica, which ran iotDevice -> configSecret -> fileServer. One block is not enough: the fileServer route to dbReplica and the browserStore/jumpHost routes share no blockable node, so no single step cuts both.\"}\n```"
